WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
- Please welcome the
one and only Adam Scott.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.357
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:09.248
- [Adam] Hey Drew.

00:00:09.248 --> 00:00:10.081
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:00:11.331 --> 00:00:14.090
- Oh my God, I'm such a fan of yours.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.810
I'm freaking out.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.200
- Well, it's the same right back at ya.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.750
I'm such a big fan of yours

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.100
and have been my whole life, essentially.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.820
- I read in some research,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.860
is it true that you have
watched "Sex in the City:

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.577
And Just Like That"?

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:33.940
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.240
I watched "Sex and the City"

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.680
when it was on originally like we all did

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.040
and then I got COVID last February,

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.060
so I got COVID classic,

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.030
like I got the original COVID,

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.380
like pre-vaccine COVID

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:56.250
and was trapped in an
apartment by myself in New York

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:01.780
and just watched all of "Sex
in the City" in like two days

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.830
and hadn't seen it in
20 years or something

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.690
and it is incredible.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.040
It's incredible what they were doing

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.973
and so far ahead of their time.

00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:12.820
It's a terrific show.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.170
- Okay, so are you a Carrie, a Samantha,

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.253
a Charlotte or a Miranda?

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.450
- I feel like I'm a Miranda probably.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.100
- Oh my God, I've become a Miranda.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:24.960
- You have.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.031
- Not the "And Just Like That" Miranda,

00:01:28.031 --> 00:01:31.203
but the "Sex and the City" Miranda.

00:01:31.203 --> 00:01:33.510
- That's the Miranda
I am as well, I think.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:34.900
- Okay, perfect.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.190
I like the "And Just Like That" Miranda,

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.780
and in fact, Cynthia Nixon

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.280
came on the show to talk about it, I love,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.960
I liked "And Just Like That"

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.600
because at first I was like,

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.200
I want my old "Sex in the City"

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.770
and then I was like,
what am I talking about?

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:50.010
We're all older, we're not the same,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.750
they're moving on, I need to
too and then I got on board.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.340
- Yeah, me too and I also
felt a little protective of it

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.880
and that people were really
quick to jump all over a show

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.520
starring all these women in their 50's.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.977
I feel like we should
applaud that and applaud them

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.581
putting these women on a show together.

00:02:14.581 --> 00:02:15.414
It's great.

00:02:15.414 --> 00:02:19.000
- Okay now your amazing wife,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:24.000
is it true that when your wife
first met you, she was like,

00:02:24.857 --> 00:02:28.700
"Oh no, no, no, no, you're an actor."?

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.420
- Yeah I mean it's only,

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.620
she's smart so of course she
would be a little trepidatious

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.093
dating an actor.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.690
And also one that kind of wasn't,

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:44.570
like I didn't really have
anything to show for it really.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:48.530
I was just trying to jump
from guest spot to guest spot

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.630
and had a little apartment,

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.020
like, I don't know why she dated me,

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.100
but I'm really glad she did.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.147
- Did she ever say like,

00:02:57.147 --> 00:03:01.150
"Oh, actors are typically dot dot dot

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.490
and that would be my fear?"

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.150
Did she give you any reasons

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.310
other than just being an actor?

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:10.310
- Yeah, I think kind of
full of themselves and,

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.990
I think full of themselves
and I think she's right.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:20.990
Like I think actors are
really kind of self-involved

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.090
but for good reason because
the thing we are doing

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:28.500
and the thing that we're selling is us.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.130
So it's hard not to be self-involved

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:35.620
to a certain degree as an actor but,

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.530
so I was working pretty hard

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.410
to show her that I wasn't self-involved

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.830
to prove her wrong.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.940
We were just shooting the other night,

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.070
we were shooting "Party Down"-

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.390
- Which is everyone's so excited about.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.717
You just finished shooting.

00:03:51.717 --> 00:03:53.180
"Party Down" is coming back,

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.720
it's like the cult classic,

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.610
everybody freaks out,

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.930
this is so exciting,

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.643
okay sorry, not to, I
didn't mean to interrupt.

00:04:00.643 --> 00:04:02.240
- No, no, no, not at all.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.870
We were just shooting on
Saturday night, we just finished

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.160
and Jennifer Garner's on the show now

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.150
and she and I were sitting there

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.710
and someone's getting us coffee

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.490
and asking us if we wanted a snack

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.360
and we just realized we're like babies,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.310
like actors are like toddlers

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:23.920
and everything on sets at
least is sort of done for them.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:28.920
So it is ridiculous how
pampered actors are.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.330
- It can be true,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.080
but look at you

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.720
and I'm sure your wife is so happy

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.210
that she gave you a chance

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.025
and you seem like such a good person.

00:04:39.025 --> 00:04:40.027
- Oh, thanks Drew.

00:04:40.027 --> 00:04:43.570
Well, I'm so, so glad she
gave me a chance as well.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.073
I'm very lucky.

00:04:45.073 --> 00:04:47.740
(upbeat music)

